maint/crd-drift-check.pl parse_crds() (around line 432) reads:

    my $spec_props = $schema->{properties}{spec}{properties};

For any CRD Kind whose openAPIV3Schema.properties has NO "spec" key at all
(not empty, literally absent -- e.g. Cilium v1.20.1s CiliumEndpoint
{apiVersion,kind,metadata,status}, CiliumIdentity
{apiVersion,kind,metadata,security-labels}, CiliumEndpointSlice v2alpha1
{apiVersion,kind,metadata,endpoints,namespace}), this chained hash read
autovivifies $schema->{properties}{spec} into an empty hashref {} as a Perl
side effect of the intermediate dereference -- even though it is only being
read, never assigned. $spec_props itself still comes out undef/0 (has_spec_schema
correctly 0), so the PLAIN REPORT (--provider X) is unaffected. But $schema is
the SAME hashref later handed to IO::K8s::CRD->generate() for --render/
--render-dir/--check (render_gvk() reuses $u->{doc} from parse_crds, never
re-parsing the manifest) -- so the corrupted properties now has a
properties.spec => {} entry that never existed upstream. AutoGen renders
that as a spurious `k8s spec => Str;` attribute with no upstream basis
("invents a field").

Repro (confirmed against Cilium v1.20.1 cached manifests in this worktree,
crd-step4 branch):

  perl maint/crd-drift-check.pl --provider Cilium --dir spec/crd/Cilium/v1.20.1 \
    --render-dir /tmp/out
  cat /tmp/out/IO/K8s/Cilium/V2/CiliumEndpoint.pm
  # -> k8s spec => Str;  (upstream CiliumEndpoint has NO spec property at all)

Confirmed via a standalone script that loads the manifest directly and calls
IO::K8s::CRD->generate() without going through parse_crds() at all: no
phantom spec field, status renders correctly and fully.

Fix: in parse_crds(), read spec existence without the chained autoviv, e.g.

    my $spec_schema = $schema->{properties} && exists $schema->{properties}{spec}
        ? $schema->{properties}{spec} : undef;
    my $spec_props = $spec_schema ? $spec_schema->{properties} : undef;

or operate on a shallow-cloned $schema before this read so the mutation
(if any) never reaches the shared doc. Blocks a clean --check MATCH for any
current/future D5 provider that has a Kind with no spec property at all
(Cilium: CiliumEndpoint, CiliumIdentity, CiliumEndpointSlice worked around
by hand in task B-Cilium, documented in maint/crd-render/Cilium.yaml and the
task report -- 3 files expected DIFFERS until this is fixed).
